<id/17/1709/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Canoes"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_metal_machinery_hardware/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "a rudely formed boat, shaped out of the trunk of a tree by cutting or burning; also a skin or bark boat used by uncivilized natives. *See WOODSKIN. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 78]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_metal_machinery_hardware; processing_state=manufactured): Vehicles and craft (wagons, gigs, canoes), cf. Carriages and Carts. Layer-1 observations: 6 rows, 1837–1842. Series: CSP_Canadian_Exports_BlankSeries (inferred, series not printed) ×6. Units: Number ×6. Top routes: Montreal and Quebec → Great Britain ×5; Montreal and Quebec → British North America ×1."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "1709" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Canoes"@en ;
